<title>FRANCE: Chirac wishes &quot;Dear Boris&quot; well.</title>
<headline>Chirac wishes &quot;Dear Boris&quot; well.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac sent a get-well-soon message to Russian President Boris Yeltsin on Tuesday, saying he was glad Yeltsin's heart surgery had gone well.</p>
<p>In a message addressed to &quot;Mr President, Dear Boris&quot;, Chirac said: &quot;I was very pleased to learn that your operation took place in the best conditions&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;I send you my warmest wishes for a quick recovery and hope you have a very good convalescence,&quot; Chirac said in the message, released by his office.</p>
<p>The Kremlin said that Yeltsin's seven-hour multiple bypass operation ended successfully.</p>
</text>
